WEBVTT

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:20.411
I set my sights far away...

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:34.532
Over and over,
I call out your name...

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:51.145
Beyond time and the heavens...

00:00:52.218 --> 00:01:05.757
I want to say I'm protecting you...

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:19.034
Now, a miracle is about to be
created upon this planet.

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:36.129
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:38.865
Earth Maiden Arjuna
Kinou no ame wa higashi no machi ni

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:42.769
Kinou no ame wa higashi no machi ni

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:47.729
Tsumetai hoshi wo furaseta

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:55.081
Kanashii kimi wa hitori de
shizuka ni

00:01:55.081 --> 00:02:01.384
Atashi no daisuki na uta
wo kuchizusamu

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:07.794
Ikanakucha fukai kurayami ni

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:10.797
Mayoikonda kare wo

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:14.824
Daremo tasukete kurenai

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:20.206
Atashi nara itoshisa dake de

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:23.176
Donna basho e demo

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:27.614
Mayowanai de hashitte yukeru

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:32.719
Dakara ooki na koe de

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:39.522
Nandomo atashi no namae wo yonde

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:57.977
Episode 10: The Flickering Genes

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:53.732
Oshima

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:58.127
Don't worry?

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:02.064
But look at the stories
in all the magazines!

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:05.202
Is the laboratory really safe?

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:07.709
Tell me, dear!

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:13.947
Uh, Tokio.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:23.263
Uh, your father came home
to change a while ago.

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:25.064
Would you like to have
breakfast together?

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.554
Well? Tokio?!

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.563
He's still in high school.

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:32.034
Where was he all night long?

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:33.804
You don't know?

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:36.843
Nevermind me.
I wish you'd just keep him in line!

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:37.810
I'm going out!

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:04.395
How am I supposed to
approach him about this?

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:09.836
Please take a look here.

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:13.179
The trees in this area
have clearly changed color.

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:16.046
There are even some
that have decomposed.

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:18.184
Based on reports of
bacterial contamination...

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:20.753
...in the magazines...

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:23.289
...we talked to the man in charge
of Bio Alpha Laboratories.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.223
General Manager of Administration
Bio Alpha Laboratories, Inc.
Akio Oshima

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:26.759
Oshima?

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.728
I don't understand why
we are being accused of this.

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:30.663
I don't understand why
we are being accused of this.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:32.265
We have absolutely nothing...

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:36.133
...to do with the problem
of trees dying in the area.

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:43.571
Tokio...!

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:47.679
This laboratory is fully
equipped with safety systems...

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:48.548
...to ensure that we won't be...

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:49.849
- Why, Tokio?
...accused of another...

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:52.511
Tokio, Tokio, huh?

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:56.681
Chris, is Tokio going to be
in some kind of danger?

00:05:57.523 --> 00:05:58.285
Well?

00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:01.123
What have you seen so far?

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:02.689
There you go again.

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:05.894
Why can't you just
be straight with me?

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:08.358
Nevermind.

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:10.329
I better get in touch with Tokio.

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:12.329
I guess it's no use.

00:06:12.839 --> 00:06:14.431
What do you mean, "no use?"

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:17.705
I guess you won't know
until the world is destroyed.

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:19.545
I'm going to save Tokio...

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:22.105
...even if I have to do it myself!

00:06:34.594 --> 00:06:35.628
Where are you now?

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:36.617
Ju-Juna...?

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:38.092
Where are you?

00:06:38.798 --> 00:06:40.197
Uh, well, I'm at home.

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:43.128
Well, actually, I...

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:48.703
Does your father work at a place
called Bio Alpha Laboratories?

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:49.272
Huh?

00:06:49.976 --> 00:06:50.499
Well?

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.707
Sure, he works there.

00:06:54.313 --> 00:06:56.304
So, that man IS Tokio's...

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:59.174
Maybe I can do something
about this now.

00:07:00.386 --> 00:07:02.081
Hey, what's the matter?

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:04.720
Tokio, listen up.

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:07.021
Don't leave your house today.

00:07:07.727 --> 00:07:08.091
See ya.

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:10.458
Huh? W-Wait a minute.

00:07:12.665 --> 00:07:13.723
What the heck was that?

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:19.802
Why is it always like this?

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:23.933
Out shopping, huh?

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:37.123
Bio Alpha Laboratory's secret
experiment on a deadly bacteria

00:07:37.123 --> 00:07:39.182
That's why she was
asking about Dad.

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:40.950
Don't tell me she's...

00:08:02.849 --> 00:08:04.851
I'm Oshima.

00:08:04.851 --> 00:08:06.252
Nice to meet you.

00:08:06.252 --> 00:08:10.052
I'm Juna Ariyoshi,
a friend of Tokio's.

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:19.631
It's dangerous here. Everyone
has to evacuate.

00:08:21.133 --> 00:08:23.158
It's true!
Please believe me!

00:08:26.806 --> 00:08:29.604
What did my son tell you?

00:08:29.909 --> 00:08:33.675
I didn't come here because
Tokio asked me to.

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:37.240
I don't know what you're
talking about.

00:08:37.617 --> 00:08:40.950
In any case, there's
no danger here.

00:08:42.221 --> 00:08:43.051
Tokio!

00:08:44.123 --> 00:08:45.021
Tokio.

00:08:46.092 --> 00:08:48.583
I told you not to leave your house!

00:08:50.596 --> 00:08:52.188
What's this article?

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:56.728
Do you know about dioxins?

00:08:58.037 --> 00:08:58.867
Uh, yes.

00:08:59.372 --> 00:09:03.209
It's a deadly toxin used as a defoliating
agent during the Vietnam War.

00:09:03.209 --> 00:09:05.344
There is something
that can break down...

00:09:05.344 --> 00:09:07.039
...that dioxin and
make it harmless.

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:08.577
What do you think it is?

00:09:09.882 --> 00:09:11.417
Mushrooms.

00:09:11.417 --> 00:09:12.315
Mushrooms?

00:09:12.718 --> 00:09:16.122
For example, a decomposing type
of bacteria in mushrooms...

00:09:16.122 --> 00:09:18.147
...has the ability to
eliminate the dioxin.

00:09:18.457 --> 00:09:21.327
The bacteria we have here
is of that type.

00:09:21.327 --> 00:09:23.029
Don't listen to him, Juna!

00:09:23.029 --> 00:09:25.164
They're using genetic
engineering...

00:09:25.164 --> 00:09:27.689
...in order to create some kind of
dangerous bacteria!

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:29.902
Are you talking about PDB?

00:09:29.902 --> 00:09:31.267
PDB...?

00:09:32.071 --> 00:09:35.097
It's short for Petrochemical
Decomposition Bacteria.

00:09:35.408 --> 00:09:38.969
It decomposes anything
made with petrochemicals.

00:09:39.278 --> 00:09:41.881
So, what's so dangerous
about that?

00:09:41.881 --> 00:09:42.540
Uh...

00:09:45.318 --> 00:09:47.411
It's just a second-hand rumor.

00:09:48.955 --> 00:09:50.122
But...

00:09:50.122 --> 00:09:51.657
...doesn't genetic engineering...

00:09:51.657 --> 00:09:54.990
...result in new life forms
that don't exist naturally?

00:09:55.528 --> 00:09:57.296
There were always...

00:09:57.296 --> 00:10:00.527
...micro-organisms in nature capable
of breaking down petroleum.

00:10:01.334 --> 00:10:04.403
All we're trying to do
is create bacteria...

00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:07.974
...through genetic engineering
that can be used to deal with...

00:10:07.974 --> 00:10:09.942
...the full range of
petrochemical substances.

00:10:11.644 --> 00:10:12.338
But, Juna.

00:10:12.645 --> 00:10:15.181
It says they have neither
the manpower nor...

00:10:15.181 --> 00:10:17.116
...the facilities to carry out
that work.

00:10:17.116 --> 00:10:20.381
They say that without
even checking.

00:10:21.787 --> 00:10:23.689
All the media is interested in...

00:10:23.689 --> 00:10:26.317
...is finding stories that
stir up public debate.

00:10:26.659 --> 00:10:29.253
There are no problems
with our facilities.

00:10:29.895 --> 00:10:30.997
But...

00:10:30.997 --> 00:10:33.399
...what if something unexpected
were to happen here?

00:10:33.399 --> 00:10:34.024
That's right!

00:10:34.266 --> 00:10:36.469
Are you going to be able to
take responsibility?!

00:10:36.469 --> 00:10:37.595
Responsibility?!

00:10:38.137 --> 00:10:41.140
Look, I just bought you a
new motorcycle the other day!

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:41.902
What?!

00:10:45.311 --> 00:10:45.800
What?

00:10:46.912 --> 00:10:48.402
Aren't you satisfied
with the motorcycle?

00:10:51.517 --> 00:10:53.314
You're always like that!

00:10:56.355 --> 00:10:59.153
I think I give you plenty
of allowance money.

00:10:59.525 --> 00:11:00.926
Always money, huh?

00:11:00.926 --> 00:11:02.695
Why don't you work, then?

00:11:02.695 --> 00:11:04.096
Work?

00:11:04.096 --> 00:11:06.291
You can't even keep
a part-time job.

00:11:06.966 --> 00:11:10.136
I had to quit, thanks to
your job transfer.

00:11:10.136 --> 00:11:13.005
You always blame others.

00:11:13.005 --> 00:11:16.406
How many times did we move
and I change schools?

00:11:16.909 --> 00:11:18.711
There was no way to avoid it.

00:11:18.711 --> 00:11:19.712
Work is important!

00:11:19.712 --> 00:11:22.415
You hardly ever came
home from work.

00:11:22.415 --> 00:11:24.280
...and left Mom and I alone.

00:11:25.184 --> 00:11:28.054
It's because I worked much
harder than others...

00:11:28.054 --> 00:11:30.045
...so that you can have such a lifestyle!

00:11:43.736 --> 00:11:44.970
You just figured that
giving me things...

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:47.063
...was all you had to do.

00:11:48.674 --> 00:11:51.544
It's because you didn't realize that,
that Mom took off!

00:11:51.544 --> 00:11:53.713
If you're going to complain
like that...

00:11:53.713 --> 00:11:56.181
...maybe you should've
gone with her!

00:12:15.935 --> 00:12:19.098
Earth Maiden Arjuna

00:12:26.545 --> 00:12:29.537
I think you should go home,
Tokio.

00:12:30.583 --> 00:12:34.485
I'm going to try talking
to your father again.

00:12:35.121 --> 00:12:37.289
Is that monster going
to attack this place?

00:12:37.289 --> 00:12:37.778
Huh?!

00:12:38.324 --> 00:12:39.291
I thought so...

00:12:40.593 --> 00:12:42.458
So, I guess I'm in the way.

00:12:42.862 --> 00:12:44.295
That's not it.

00:12:46.699 --> 00:12:50.035
I mean, I don't have
the power of Chris, after all.

00:12:50.035 --> 00:12:52.265
I'll just get in the way.

00:12:52.738 --> 00:12:53.636
No.

00:12:54.373 --> 00:12:57.069
I'm not good enough
no matter what I do.

00:12:58.277 --> 00:13:00.040
That's not so, Tokio.

00:13:12.825 --> 00:13:15.361
I never thought the
decomposition rate of the PDB...

00:13:15.361 --> 00:13:18.023
...would double like that
in an instant.

00:13:19.632 --> 00:13:22.294
What genes did you
incorporate into it this time?

00:13:23.002 --> 00:13:24.299
What do you think?

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:26.835
Some virus again?

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:30.334
The cancer gene BTS1.

00:13:30.743 --> 00:13:32.005
A cancer gene?!

00:13:32.711 --> 00:13:34.008
Are you sure that's safe?

00:13:34.847 --> 00:13:38.112
Everyone was very impressed
with you on TV today.

00:13:38.784 --> 00:13:41.719
They thought you handled
the media quite nicely.

00:13:42.188 --> 00:13:44.418
We'll be counting on you again.

00:13:46.826 --> 00:13:47.793
It's true.

00:13:48.394 --> 00:13:50.596
I just didn't want to
drag you into it.

00:13:50.596 --> 00:13:52.359
That's all it is.

00:13:53.566 --> 00:13:55.234
Even so...

00:13:55.234 --> 00:13:58.032
...I might not be the man
best suited to you.

00:13:58.671 --> 00:14:01.469
I'm never any help to you
when you need me the most.

00:14:02.675 --> 00:14:04.040
Tokio...

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:07.737
I can't even relate
to my own father.

00:14:09.849 --> 00:14:11.476
That's because you don't
reach him.

00:14:12.751 --> 00:14:15.421
Your voice doesn't
reach your father.

00:14:15.421 --> 00:14:20.051
No, even his voice
doesn't reach you.

00:14:23.295 --> 00:14:25.354
What about you?

00:14:25.664 --> 00:14:27.733
Did your voice...

00:14:27.733 --> 00:14:29.257
...reach your father?

00:14:32.838 --> 00:14:33.930
I guess it didn't.

00:14:34.306 --> 00:14:36.740
I guess I'm not one to talk.

00:14:39.411 --> 00:14:40.045
A Raaja!

00:14:40.045 --> 00:14:41.569
What?!

00:14:43.182 --> 00:14:43.739
What?!

00:14:45.451 --> 00:14:46.118
Calm down!

00:14:46.118 --> 00:14:47.553
Let's get our
decontamination suits!

00:14:47.553 --> 00:14:49.188
You go and check on Labs Two and Three!

00:14:49.188 --> 00:14:50.212
Y-Yes, sir!

00:14:53.425 --> 00:14:54.221
Stay away!

00:14:54.426 --> 00:14:56.395
I don't want to fight you anymore!

00:14:56.395 --> 00:14:57.589
Juna!

00:14:58.397 --> 00:14:58.795
Tokio!

00:14:59.498 --> 00:15:01.400
Tokio, get out of here quick!

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:03.535
How can you expect me to
run away by myself?!

00:15:03.535 --> 00:15:05.730
Don't worry about your father!

00:15:05.938 --> 00:15:07.303
I'll rescue him!

00:15:07.873 --> 00:15:09.408
Am I that useless...?

00:15:09.408 --> 00:15:10.397
Hurry!

00:15:16.415 --> 00:15:16.949
No!

00:15:16.949 --> 00:15:18.314
Don't go in there!

00:15:22.454 --> 00:15:23.284
Ashura!

00:15:28.694 --> 00:15:29.490
I have no choice!

00:15:30.062 --> 00:15:31.256
Dad!

00:15:31.664 --> 00:15:32.790
Where are you?!

00:15:35.467 --> 00:15:36.900
Dad!

00:15:38.504 --> 00:15:39.493
Tokio!

00:15:41.941 --> 00:15:43.108
Excuse me!

00:15:43.108 --> 00:15:44.310
Where's Mr. Oshima?!

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:45.277
Who are you?!

00:15:45.277 --> 00:15:46.779
You shouldn't be here!

00:15:46.779 --> 00:15:48.178
Just tell me!

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:50.983
He's in Lab One, straight that way
and to the left.

00:15:50.983 --> 00:15:51.550
Right!

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:52.448
Hey!

00:16:01.827 --> 00:16:02.561
Now where...?

00:16:02.561 --> 00:16:03.391
Dad!

00:16:03.696 --> 00:16:04.563
What?!

00:16:04.563 --> 00:16:05.998
What are you doing?!

00:16:05.998 --> 00:16:07.800
Some monster is
attacking this place!

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:09.301
Monster?!

00:16:09.301 --> 00:16:11.470
Stop talking nonsense!
Just get out of here!

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:13.062
It's dangerous here!

00:16:14.106 --> 00:16:15.674
So, it is dangerous here!

00:16:15.674 --> 00:16:17.309
What do you think danger is?!

00:16:17.309 --> 00:16:20.412
Do you think we can beat the
competition without taking risks?!

00:16:20.412 --> 00:16:21.936
Competition?

00:16:22.381 --> 00:16:23.871
What are you talking about?

00:16:24.183 --> 00:16:25.878
At this rate, even your life is...

00:16:26.251 --> 00:16:26.910
Tokio...

00:16:27.653 --> 00:16:29.154
Don't be stupid!

00:16:29.154 --> 00:16:32.491
How much do you think we have
invested in this project?!

00:16:32.491 --> 00:16:34.186
Money, money, money!

00:16:35.995 --> 00:16:37.262
No!

00:16:37.262 --> 00:16:39.965
I have a responsibility to
the project and the company!

00:16:39.965 --> 00:16:42.134
Forget about the company!

00:16:42.134 --> 00:16:44.398
Isn't your responsibility
right now to protect people?

00:16:46.205 --> 00:16:49.971
You still despise me because of
what happened to your mother?!

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:52.370
That's not it.

00:16:52.845 --> 00:16:54.646
You just want to get back at me!

00:16:54.646 --> 00:16:56.281
I said that's not it!

00:16:56.281 --> 00:16:57.449
You want to get back at me!

00:16:57.449 --> 00:16:58.939
That's not it!

00:16:59.952 --> 00:17:01.078
What is this...?

00:17:02.421 --> 00:17:06.025
Red and red.

00:17:06.025 --> 00:17:08.459
Blue and blue.

00:17:17.136 --> 00:17:20.469
Are these the colors of emotions?

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:26.400
They're the same.

00:17:26.912 --> 00:17:29.181
Both Tokio and his
father's emotions...

00:17:29.181 --> 00:17:30.910
...are moving together.

00:17:31.283 --> 00:17:32.682
But then, why...?

00:17:33.118 --> 00:17:35.586
But why don't the
words get through?

00:17:40.025 --> 00:17:42.227
Why can't you believe me
even a bit?!

00:17:42.227 --> 00:17:45.030
I've done what I could!

00:17:45.030 --> 00:17:47.089
Why are you so unsatisfied?!

00:18:05.584 --> 00:18:08.053
It wasn't just Tokio...

00:18:08.053 --> 00:18:09.354
...even his father was...

00:18:09.354 --> 00:18:10.753
That's why...

00:18:11.023 --> 00:18:13.759
Why won't you listen to me?

00:18:13.759 --> 00:18:16.195
And you call yourself my father?!

00:18:16.195 --> 00:18:16.962
No.

00:18:16.962 --> 00:18:18.497
You are father and son.

00:18:18.497 --> 00:18:19.464
Juna!

00:18:19.731 --> 00:18:20.425
What?

00:18:20.999 --> 00:18:25.070
Your emotions
are exactly the same.

00:18:25.070 --> 00:18:26.405
They're a match.

00:18:26.405 --> 00:18:27.770
A match?

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:29.475
My father and I?

00:18:29.475 --> 00:18:31.376
And not just feelings.

00:18:31.376 --> 00:18:32.778
It is all the same.

00:18:32.778 --> 00:18:35.280
When your father was a child,
just like you...

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:39.410
...his father bought him
all kinds of things.

00:18:39.918 --> 00:18:42.182
Dad got stuff, too?

00:18:43.355 --> 00:18:46.722
You must have been lonely
with just that.

00:18:47.759 --> 00:18:49.124
Lonely?

00:18:49.962 --> 00:18:53.866
That is the proof of how much
my father loved me.

00:18:53.866 --> 00:18:57.302
The things he bought me were
what bonded father to son.

00:18:57.302 --> 00:18:58.537
That's why I...

